            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0743" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Great Britain/292: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain (Mellon)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-26T14:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1932—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. Department’s circular February 26th, 11 A.M. Treasury draft of agreement to
                    carry out Congressional Resolution regarding debt postponement has been handed
                    to British Ambassador<anchor n="52" xml:id="d418-f1"/> today. Treasury anxious
                    to expedite action. Department does not desire that you make special call on
                    officials regarding this but in connection with other matters hopes you will
                    find opportunity to inquire whether prompt action can be expected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
